    bc: Prototype zero-inline COW storage as an ownership control
    
    Retain current vector/COW arithmetic while sending nonempty coefficients
    to heap storage. This supplies a contemporary control for the three-limb
    hybrid without relabeling a historical executable as the current source.
    Keep a valid empty pointer range with one unused local limb.
    
    The prototype is not an adoption decision. CLI, VM, independent arithmetic
    oracle groups and all 45 quick benchmark oracles pass. Production inline
    layout assertions do not apply to this control. Compare matched release
    timings and actual process memory before choosing an ownership policy.
    
    Refs #202 and #197.

diff --git a/docs/utilities/bc-202-heap-control.md b/docs/utilities/bc-202-heap-control.md
